---
name: accordion
type: registry:ui
title: Accordion
description: A vertically stacked set of expandable sections.
dependencies:
  - bits-ui
files:
  - path: src/lib/components/ui/accordion/accordion.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/accordion/accordion.svelte"
  - path: src/lib/components/ui/accordion/accordion-item.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/accordion/accordion-item.svelte"
  - path: src/lib/components/ui/accordion/accordion-trigger.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/accordion/accordion-trigger.svelte"
  - path: src/lib/components/ui/accordion/accordion-content.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/accordion/accordion-content.svelte"
  - path: src/lib/components/ui/accordion/index.ts
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/accordion/index.ts"
---

Use `Accordion.Root`, `Accordion.Item`, `Accordion.Trigger`, and `Accordion.Content` together to build a set of collapsible sections. Set `type="single"` to allow only one open item at a time, or `"multiple"` to allow several.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import * as Accordion from "../../components/accordion";
</script>

<Accordion.Root type="single">
  <Accordion.Item value="item-1">
    <Accordion.Trigger>Is it accessible?</Accordion.Trigger>
    <Accordion.Content>Yes. It follows the WAI-ARIA design pattern.</Accordion.Content>
  </Accordion.Item>
</Accordion.Root>
```
